A||||13||Pyric||Intake mystery... will an 87 fit an 85?||||1||
Z||000000||Pyric||12-03-2001||12:13 PM||||Alright, I recently found out (thanks to Elvira) that the 87 and 88 V6 Plenums had "FIERO" engraved on them.  Mine just has a sticker  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I like the engraved one better.  Does anyone know if an 87 or 88 plenum will fit on an 85 GT?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||chester||12-03-2001||12:19 PM||||Bolts right on.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">     <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||14
Z||000002||Pyric||12-03-2001||01:18 PM||||Thanks, Just wanted to check before I went after one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||12-03-2001||02:18 PM||||yes, <B>but</B>...!<P>The vacuum hose port for the brake booster is a different size, much bigger in 87-88.  I ran into this when I put an engraved plenum on my 86 GT.  I managed to push hard enough to get the hose over the port.. probably not the best way but I had to get it done and it's held up so far.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-03-2001||03:16 PM||||Hmm, something to look at next time I'm with some Fiero people.  Is the brake booster port just a screw-in port on the plenum?  If so, you should be able to just take the one out of your old plenum and put it in the new one.  I'll take a look next time I'm with someone with a non-engraved plenum.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-03-2001||04:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>Alright, I recently found out (thanks to Elvira) that the 87 and 88 V6 Plenums had "FIERO" engraved on them.  Mine just has a sticker   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I like the engraved one better.  Does anyone know if an 87 or 88 plenum will fit on an 85 GT?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>My 86 and 1/2 GT Fastback has an engraved plenium. Probably when they started them. First of the fastbacks.<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-03-2001||06:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>Hmm, something to look at next time I'm with some Fiero people.  Is the brake booster port just a screw-in port on the plenum?  If so, you should be able to just take the one out of your old plenum and put it in the new one.  I'll take a look next time I'm with someone with a non-engraved plenum.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Standard is right on here, and the reply on the port, I'm not sure on which one or both, but one of the plenums has the port pressed in.<P> There is a difference where you can't swap ports, been there, done that type thing<P> I can check tomorrow when its light out if you want me to.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||12-04-2001||12:47 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>My 86 and 1/2 GT Fastback has an engraved plenium. Probably when they started them. First of the fastbacks.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll bet a p/o swapped that one, Aus.  That's what I had to do to my 86.5 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Oh yeah, and I'm pretty sure it's the 85-86 ports that are presssed in. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
