Z||000010||The Fieromaster||12-05-2001||11:03 AM||||87 started the engraved plenum... thats what Scott told me.. (fierokid87) when i was looking for one for myself!!  If you got it on any other year its swapped!  There wasnt any other package of any type that would offer that in 86!  ALTHOUGH ever think your engine was replaced? Perhaps with a 87!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||12-05-2001||11:09 AM||||Officially the earlier statements were correct... the '85 & '86 (including 86.5 GT's) had the stickered plenum (it's one of the only distinguishing differences between 86.5 & 87 GTs).<P>They are quite easily switched- as Standard said above- the port size is different, but not difficult to fix.  <P>I actually have an '86 Plenum on my '87 GT- no sticker... just clean on top (it's a Darrel Morse Bored-Out Plenum & TB I won at a MFF Christmas Party!)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
